webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4729034Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4738692Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4844585Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4854440Z ^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4855112Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4855946Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4856358Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4856744Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4858045Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4858590Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4858936Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4859660Z    if you are ready to continue.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4860265Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4860891Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4861882Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4862740Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4863367Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4863665Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4864017Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4864474Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4864799Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4865214Z    can use Nix.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4865382Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4865500Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4865680Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4866067Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4866552Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4870005Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4870231Z I will:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4870558Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4870903Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4871674Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4872443Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4873042Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4873366Z  - install Nix in /nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4873682Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4874139Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4874575Z    /root
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4885938Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4886734Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4898250Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4899100Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4899402Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4900695Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4901428Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4918762Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4919476Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4929618Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4930783Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4931518Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4931865Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4932147Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4932588Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4932930Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4933678Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4934083Z 
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4934275Z If you would like to
webui PHPUnit	Install Nix	2026-10-08T13:27:15.4934743Z see the output, try like this:
